images.prompt:
Create a premium historical Chinese city-builder UI BUTTON ART atlas for an original Godot game. Square highest resolution (2048x2048 preferred), strict regular 4 COLUMNS by 4 ROWS grid with EXACTLY SIXTEEN separate complete buttons. Every cell at least 256px, every button centered with generous clear transparent margin. TRUE TRANSPARENT background outside each individual button. All 16 buttons identical square footprint and consistent size. No words, letters, numbers, captions, grid lines, labels, extra items or landscape.
Style: beautifully hand-painted miniature crafted interface objects, exquisite bronze relief and antique warm gold on small dark walnut plaques. Low-profile square plaques with gently chamfered corners, thin aged bronze edging and subtle hand-carved wood grain. The central pictorial symbol is large and immediately legible, occupies most of the plaque. Sharp details and clean silhouettes, light from upper left. Rich tactile craft, controlled gold highlights, muted jade accents. NOT flat vector line icons, NOT emojis, NOT glossy plastic, no glow or hazy shadows. The button itself is front-facing and flat enough for interface readability; raised metal pictorial elements may have subtle realistic depth.
EXACT ROW-MAJOR ORDER:
ROW 1:
1 BUILD: crossed small carpenter's mallet and timber framing-square, antique gold;
2 ROAD: a short winding paved cobblestone path symbol in a raised gold relief;
3 WORLD: a small engraved bronze globe sphere within a thin ring, with jade-blue seas;
4 VIEW: an elegant bronze spyglass telescope angled upward.
ROW 2:
5 MENU: three large clearly separated horizontal carved bronze bars;
6 INVENTORY: a handsome small open wooden storage chest showing folded cloth and a grain sack;
7 TASK: a cream parchment scroll and a large gold checkmark in front;
8 SAVE: a gold arrow pointing DOWN into a small bronze archive chest, very clearly downward.
ROW 3:
9 LOAD: a gold arrow pointing UP out of the same style bronze archive chest, very clearly upward;
10 CENTER: a small geometric four-pointed compass target, central gold diamond and four inward pointing corners;
11 ZOOM IN: a bronze magnifying glass with a clearly visible large PLUS-shaped gold symbol inside the lens;
12 ZOOM OUT: a bronze magnifying glass with a clearly visible large MINUS-shaped gold bar inside the lens.
ROW 4:
13 DAY: a radiant round gold SUN with a strong circular disc and eight engraved rays;
14 NIGHT: a silver-gold CRESCENT MOON and two tiny stars against dark jade;
15 DEMOLISH: a small carpenter's pickaxe striking and cracking a stone block, restrained red-bronze accent;
16 CANCEL: a large robust diagonal X made of two crossed antique bronze strips, clear and unmistakable.
All sixteen standalone buttons have the exact same visual system, dimensions and border thickness. The contents differ as listed. Painted original game art, no existing game UI copied.
